From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:00:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ionic: don't leave a failed XDP frame in the Tx descriptor info

ionic_xdp_post_frame() records the frame and the XDP action in the Tx
descriptor info before it maps the frags. If mapping a frag of an
XDP_REDIRECT frame fails it unmaps what it had mapped and returns -EIO,
but leaves desc_info->xdpf and desc_info->act set. The queue head has not
moved, so the next thing sent on that queue uses the same descriptor
info.

If that is an skb, ionic_tx() and ionic_tx_tso() only set desc_info->skb.
When the descriptor completes, ionic_tx_clean() sees xdpf set and takes
the XDP branch: the stale frame, which the caller of ndo_xdp_xmit()
already freed when it got the error, is returned a second time, and the
skb is never freed.

Record the frame and the action only once all the buffers are mapped.
The unmap in the error path only needs nbufs.

Found by code inspection; the failure needs a multi-buffer XDP_REDIRECT
into ionic and a DMA mapping error, and was not reproduced.

Fixes: 5377805dc1c0 ("ionic: implement xdp frags support")

[ rocm-ernic: backport of patch 1/6 of the RFC series "ionic: support
  netmem TX" (based on v7.4-rc3, not posted) to v7.2.6 with patches/srq
  and patches/p4. The diff is unchanged. ]
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
index 2543a8ff8547..2733a65bd1d5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_txrx.c
@@ -335,8 +335,6 @@ static int ionic_xdp_post_frame(struct ionic_queue *q, struct xdp_frame *frame,
 	buf_info->page_offset = off;
 
 	desc_info->nbufs = 1;
-	desc_info->xdpf = frame;
-	desc_info->act = act;
 
 	if (xdp_frame_has_frags(frame)) {
 		struct ionic_txq_sg_elem *elem;
@@ -378,6 +376,9 @@ static int ionic_xdp_post_frame(struct ionic_queue *q, struct xdp_frame *frame,
 		}
 	}
 
+	desc_info->xdpf = frame;
+	desc_info->act = act;
+
 	cmd = encode_txq_desc_cmd(IONIC_TXQ_DESC_OPCODE_CSUM_NONE,
 				  0, (desc_info->nbufs - 1), buf_info->dma_addr);
 	desc->cmd = cpu_to_le64(cmd);
-- 
